{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "RadGuard",
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.0.dev0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "pixels.ambiguous-geometry",
              "name": "PixelsAmbiguousGeometry",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Conflicting image dimensions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Rows, Columns, Samples per Pixel, Number of Frames or Bits Allocated appears more than once with different values, so readers that keep different copies decode the same pixel bytes with different dimensions."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "Rows, Columns, Samples per Pixel, Number of Frames or Bits Allocated appears more than once with different values, so readers that keep different copies decode the same pixel bytes with different dimensions.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsambiguous-geometry",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-436"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "436",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.analysis-incomplete",
              "name": "PixelsAnalysisIncomplete",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Frames beyond the inspection budget"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Compressed frames beyond the per-file reassembly budget were not inspected."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Part of the file was not inspected, so the verdict for it is partial. Inspect the reported range with other tools. A file that deliberately exhausts analysis budgets should be treated as hostile.",
                "markdown": "Compressed frames beyond the per-file reassembly budget were not inspected.\n\n**What to do:** Part of the file was not inspected, so the verdict for it is partial. Inspect the reported range with other tools. A file that deliberately exhausts analysis budgets should be treated as hostile."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsanalysis-incomplete",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "incomplete"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.codec-mismatch",
              "name": "PixelsCodecMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Frame is not the codec its transfer syntax declares"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A frame does not start with its codec's start marker, so decoders either fail or, if they sniff the content, decode something else. Critical when the frame is an executable."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "A frame does not start with its codec's start marker, so decoders either fail or, if they sniff the content, decode something else. Critical when the frame is an executable.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelscodec-mismatch",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-436"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "436",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.codestream-trailing-data",
              "name": "PixelsCodestreamTrailingData",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data after the end of a compressed frame"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Decoders stop at a codestream's end marker, so bytes after it are never displayed: a second hidden image, or an executable. Medium for a few unexplained bytes, critical for an executable."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden.",
                "markdown": "Decoders stop at a codestream's end marker, so bytes after it are never displayed: a second hidden image, or an executable. Medium for a few unexplained bytes, critical for an executable.\n\n**What to do:** Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelscodestream-trailing-data",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "hidden-data",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-514"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "514",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.duplicate-pixel-data",
              "name": "PixelsDuplicatePixelData",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Two images in one file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The dataset has more than one Pixel Data element. Software that keeps the first copy and software that keeps the last display different images from the same file, so a radiologist's viewer and an AI pipeline can be shown different scans."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "The dataset has more than one Pixel Data element. Software that keeps the first copy and software that keeps the last display different images from the same file, so a radiologist's viewer and an AI pipeline can be shown different scans.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsduplicate-pixel-data",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-436"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "9.5"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "436",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.embedded-file",
              "name": "PixelsEmbeddedFile",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "File stored as image pixels"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The declared image area contains a recognised file format. Viewers render it as noise, and nothing that only displays images will notice. Severity follows what was found: critical for executables."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Quarantine the file and keep it away from anything that could run or extract the embedded content. Extract the payload at the reported offset for malware analysis, find out how the file entered the archive, and check other files from the same source. Re-saving the file in a viewer is not a fix: it may keep the payload, and it destroys evidence.",
                "markdown": "The declared image area contains a recognised file format. Viewers render it as noise, and nothing that only displays images will notice. Severity follows what was found: critical for executables.\n\n**What to do:** Quarantine the file and keep it away from anything that could run or extract the embedded content. Extract the payload at the reported offset for malware analysis, find out how the file entered the archive, and check other files from the same source. Re-saving the file in a viewer is not a fix: it may keep the payload, and it destroys evidence."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsembedded-file",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "malware",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-506"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "9.5"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "506",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.encoding-mismatch",
              "name": "PixelsEncodingMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pixel Data encoding contradicts the transfer syntax"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Compressed transfer syntaxes require encapsulated Pixel Data and native ones require a single value. A mismatch sends decoders down different code paths for the same bytes."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "Compressed transfer syntaxes require encapsulated Pixel Data and native ones require a single value. A mismatch sends decoders down different code paths for the same bytes.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.\n\n**References:**\n- <https://dicom.nema.org/medical/dicom/current/output/chtml/part05/sect_A.4.html>"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsencoding-mismatch",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-436"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              },
              "relationships": [
                {
                  "target": {
                    "id": "436",
                    "toolComponent": {
                      "name": "CWE",
                      "guid": "ec480a2c-8267-5d90-affc-401687cd64b0"
                    }
                  },
                  "kinds": [
                    "relevant"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.hidden-frames",
              "name": "PixelsHiddenFrames",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "More frames than declared"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Encapsulated Pixel Data holds more frames than Number of Frames declares; decoders that trust the header show fewer frames than decoders that walk the fragments."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "Encapsulated Pixel Data holds more frames than Number of Frames declares; decoders that trust the header show fewer frames than decoders that walk the fragments.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.\n\n**References:**\n- <https://dicom.nema.org/medical/dicom/current/output/chtml/part05/sect_A.4.html>"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelshidden-frames",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "differential",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-436"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
