                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.malformed-codestream",
              "name": "PixelsMalformedCodestream",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Malformed compressed frame"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A JPEG, JPEG-LS, JPEG 2000 or RLE frame breaks its own format's structure. Malformed codestreams are the input class behind many image decoder memory-safety bugs."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Open the file only with current, sandboxed decoders: this is the input class behind decoder memory-safety bugs. Quarantine it and trace its source, because crafted headers like this rarely occur by accident.",
                "markdown": "A JPEG, JPEG-LS, JPEG 2000 or RLE frame breaks its own format's structure. Malformed codestreams are the input class behind many image decoder memory-safety bugs.\n\n**What to do:** Open the file only with current, sandboxed decoders: this is the input class behind decoder memory-safety bugs. Quarantine it and trace its source, because crafted headers like this rarely occur by accident."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsmalformed-codestream",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "memory-safety"
                ],
                "precision": "high",
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "pixels.missing-frames",
              "name": "PixelsMissingFrames",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Fewer frames than declared"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Encapsulated Pixel Data holds fewer frames than Number of Frames declares; decoders that trust the header look for frames that are not there."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "Encapsulated Pixel Data holds fewer frames than Number of Frames declares; decoders that trust the header look for frames that are not there.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.\n\n**References:**\n- <https://dicom.nema.org/medical/dicom/current/output/chtml/part05/sect_A.4.html>"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsmissing-frames",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
