            {
              "id": "pixels.multiple-representations",
              "name": "PixelsMultipleRepresentations",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Integer and floating-point pixel data in one file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pixel Data and (Double) Float Pixel Data are mutually exclusive; which one is displayed depends on the software."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again.",
                "markdown": "Pixel Data and (Double) Float Pixel Data are mutually exclusive; which one is displayed depends on the software.\n\n**What to do:** Different DICOM software can read this file differently, so no single viewer's rendering can be trusted. Compare what the viewer, the PACS and any AI pipeline actually show; to normalise the study, re-acquire it from the source, or rewrite it with a strict toolkit and scan it again."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#pixelsmultiple-representations",
