            {
              "id": "private.creator-invalid",
              "name": "PrivateCreatorInvalid",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Malformed Private Creator"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A Private Creator is empty, not LO, too long or contains control characters, so readers that match creators by name cannot recognise the block."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Usually a buggy or non-conforming writer rather than an attack. Note the producing software (Implementation Class UID and Version Name in the File Meta Information) and report the defect to its vendor if it recurs.",
                "markdown": "A Private Creator is empty, not LO, too long or contains control characters, so readers that match creators by name cannot recognise the block.\n\n**What to do:** Usually a buggy or non-conforming writer rather than an attack. Note the producing software (Implementation Class UID and Version Name in the File Meta Information) and report the defect to its vendor if it recurs.\n\n**References:**\n- <https://dicom.nema.org/medical/dicom/current/output/chtml/part05/sect_7.8.html>"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#privatecreator-invalid",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "conformance"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "private.data-after-stream",
              "name": "PrivateDataAfterStream",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data hidden after a compressed stream"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Bytes follow the end of a compressed private value. Decompressors stop at the end of the stream, so nothing that reads the value normally sees them."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden.",
                "markdown": "Bytes follow the end of a compressed private value. Decompressors stop at the end of the stream, so nothing that reads the value normally sees them.\n\n**What to do:** Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#privatedata-after-stream",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "hidden-data",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-514"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5"
