            {
              "id": "structure.nonzero-padding",
              "name": "StructureNonzeroPadding",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Data hidden in trailing padding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "(FFFC,FFFC) Data Set Trailing Padding has no meaning (PS3.10 7.2) and readers skip it unread, so non-zero content in it is invisible to every DICOM tool. High or critical when it contains a recognised file."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden.",
                "markdown": "(FFFC,FFFC) Data Set Trailing Padding has no meaning (PS3.10 7.2) and readers skip it unread, so non-zero content in it is invisible to every DICOM tool. High or critical when it contains a recognised file.\n\n**What to do:** Extract the bytes at the reported offset (`radguard map` shows the file's layout) and identify them. Conforming software never stores data where readers do not look, so the content is either a writer bug or deliberately hidden.\n\n**References:**\n- <https://dicom.nema.org/medical/dicom/current/output/chtml/part10/chapter_7.html>"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Aahil-Riyaz/radguard/blob/main/docs/rules.md#structurenonzero-padding",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "hidden-data",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-514"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5"
